intelligence officials say attacks like  those in Paris require significant  logistical expertise but not necessarily  all that much money  Islamic state seemingly has both the  group has ambitions to be an independent  state and today controls large portions  of both Syria and Iraq and even though  the attacks in Paris may not have needed  much capital sustaining an enormous  global operation does so here's a look  at how Islamic state makes its money in  the territories that occupies the  group's members rob banks levy taxes on  transited Goods and extort cash from  ordinary citizens according to data from  alleged Islamic state financial  documents confiscation otherwise known  as theft makes up almost 45% of the  group's revenue that totals about 3.7  million dollars a month taxation  accounts for about 24% almost two  million dollars a month the Islamic  state controls much of water on Syria's  oil fields and refineries the US  Treasury Department estimates that  before the American bombing campaign on  Syrian refineries began in September  2014 Islamic state was earning as much  as two million dollars a day from oil  sales the group was able to rebuild and  adapt its facilities and in November  2015 the US Treasury said the group was  still earning 40 million dollars a month  in oil sales that's 1.3 million dollars  a day  Islamic state militants have taken  thousands of civilians hostage some of  them are executed but many more are  ransomed for financial gain the US  Treasury Department estimates that  Islamic state made between twenty and  forty five million dollars in kidnap and  ransom during 2014 the Islamic state  solicits money from supporters around  the world and in 2014 the US Treasury  Department estimates the group made five  million dollars from foreign donations  early in the spring of 2015 a suburban  mother from Chicago together with five  others was indicted for sending military  equipment and money to terrorist  organizations including Islamic state  and in October 2015 in Cologne Germany  members of a gang were charged with  stealing twenty-one thousand five  hundred dollars from local churches and  schools when sending that money to  Islamic state the militants now control  territory in Iraq and Syria that  historically has produced half of  Syria's wheat crop and a third of Iraq's  those fields taken with 40% of Iraq's  barley supply could earn the militants  200 million dollars a year the group's  diverse revenue streams is what sets it  apart from other terrorist organizations  like al Qaeda that group depends on a  small network of wealthy donors this  difference means that Islamic states  funds keep flowing even if individual  sources sometimes dry up but after the  Paris attacks political leaders around  the world are seriously focused on how  to permanently cut off all of the  group's revenue streams  [Music]
 

